hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"378","Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the 'aqiqah which Fatimah offered for al-Hasan and al-Husayn: ""Send a leg of it to the midwife, and eat and feed others, and do not break any of its bones."
"379","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Malik, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, that he said: Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), weighed the hair of al-Hasan, al-Husayn, Zaynab, and Umm Kulthum, and gave silver equal to its weight in charity."
"380","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ata', he said: There is no harm in making roast meat, meaning from the 'aqiqah."
